          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n\n# TODO 1: Fix the definition of hours\nhours = [1, 3, 5, 8, 10]\nscores = [27, 34, 37, 50, 58]\n\n# This line confirms how many examples the data holds:\nprint(\"Data loaded:\", len(hours), \"examples\")\n\n# This line creates a new, untrained model:\nmodel = LinearRegression()\n\n# This line trains the model on the client's data:\nmodel.fit(hours, scores)\n\n# TODO 2: Predict the value you made on paper",
